prompts
prompts for encoding queries versus encoding passages. SentenceTransformers provides this functionality through two features:
prompt dictionary via the [prompts](https://sbert.net/docs/package_reference/sentence_transformer/SentenceTransformer.html#sentence_transformers.SentenceTransformer) argument.
prompt_name](https://sbert.net/docs/package_reference/sentence_transformer/SentenceTransformer.html#sentence_transformers.SentenceTransformer.encode) argument. If the argument matches a key in the prompt dictionary, that prompt will be used automatically.
prompt_name`, I added a new `prompt_type` argument and renamed `prompt_name` to `task_name`. The other change is that `encode_queries` and `encode_corpus` now specify `query` and `passage` as their respective `prompt_type` argument, which matches SentenceTransformers&#39; default. As a side benefit, this allows instruct models to also have specific prompts for queries and passages. 

